WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.756 --> 00:00:07.874
Tom Lindqvist: Morning, Michelle. How's it going out there in Denver?

2
00:00:08.867 --> 00:00:11.869
Michelle Tran: Morning, Tom. Pretty good, busy week. How about you?

3
00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:20.931
Tom Lindqvist: Same here. I wanted to walk through where we are with the onboarding and lock down a few dates. Do you have about twenty minutes?

4
00:00:21.317 --> 00:00:25.124
Michelle Tran: Yeah, I've got the time. I've got the calendar open.

5
00:00:26.382 --> 00:00:35.786
Tom Lindqvist: Perfect. So first thing, the Genesys side. I know your team was getting the screen pop configured last week. Where did that land?

6
00:00:36.768 --> 00:00:44.867
Michelle Tran: It's set up in the test environment. We're doing a small pilot with a handful of sales reps starting Monday.

7
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:50.713
Tom Lindqvist: Okay, good. And who's the lead on that from your side?

8
00:00:52.008 --> 00:00:56.234
Michelle Tran: Dana's running the pilot, she owns the sales floor tech.

9
00:00:56.522 --> 00:01:03.614
Tom Lindqvist: Got it. I'll make sure she has my contact info in case anything comes up during the pilot week.

10
00:01:04.729 --> 00:01:08.655
Michelle Tran: That would help. She'll probably have questions about the routing piece.

11
00:01:09.627 --> 00:01:17.901
Tom Lindqvist: Sure. Now the training dates. We talked about doing two sessions for the call tracking admins. Are we still thinking the first week of November?

12
00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:25.109
Michelle Tran: First week works, but Tuesday is a holiday for some of the team. Could we do Wednesday and Thursday?

13
00:01:26.256 --> 00:01:31.637
Tom Lindqvist: Wednesday and Thursday, the fourth and fifth. What time works? We did ten in the past.

14
00:01:32.354 --> 00:01:38.361
Michelle Tran: Ten is fine. That gives people time to get through the morning queue first.

15
00:01:39.138 --> 00:01:48.265
Tom Lindqvist: I'll send the invites today. Should I include the whole admin group or just the two who are taking over the day to day?

16
00:01:49.322 --> 00:01:54.488
Michelle Tran: Include everyone. A couple of people are just watching, but they like to sit in.

17
00:01:55.672 --> 00:01:59.219
Tom Lindqvist: No problem. How many should I expect on the invite?

18
00:02:00.608 --> 00:02:01.933
Michelle Tran: Probably eight. Maybe nine.

19
00:02:02.671 --> 00:02:12.239
Tom Lindqvist: Okay. Next, user changes. I saw a ticket come through about adding a few seats on the messaging side. Is that still in motion?

20
00:02:13.586 --> 00:02:20.338
Michelle Tran: Yes, we're adding four seats for the seasonal push. Should be finalized by the end of the month.

21
00:02:20.824 --> 00:02:28.114
Tom Lindqvist: Good. I'll keep an eye out and confirm once they're active. Anything else changing on the account side?

22
00:02:29.318 --> 00:02:35.777
Michelle Tran: Not really. We're heading into the busy stretch with the holiday campaigns, so mostly just volume.

23
00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:41.450
Tom Lindqvist: Makes sense. Do you expect the call volume to shift much week over week?

24
00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:48.467
Michelle Tran: Probably up a bit starting mid-November, then it settles after the first of the year.

25
00:02:49.172 --> 00:02:56.419
Tom Lindqvist: Good to know. If it gets heavy I can check in more often. Otherwise we'll keep the monthly cadence.

26
00:02:57.604 --> 00:02:59.563
Michelle Tran: Monthly is fine for now.

27
00:03:00.686 --> 00:03:08.154
Tom Lindqvist: Last thing, the reporting walkthrough for Adobe. Do you want that bundled into the November sessions or separate?

28
00:03:08.714 --> 00:03:12.351
Michelle Tran: Separate, I think. The admins will be maxed out that week.

29
00:03:13.243 --> 00:03:17.306
Tom Lindqvist: Okay, I'll look at the week after and send some options.

30
00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:19.431
Michelle Tran: Sounds good.

31
00:03:20.495 --> 00:03:28.421
Tom Lindqvist: That's everything on my list. I'll get the invites and the Adobe options over by end of day.

32
00:03:29.517 --> 00:03:30.784
Michelle Tran: Perfect. Thanks, Tom.

33
00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:32.964
Tom Lindqvist: Thanks, Michelle. Talk soon.
